<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 domestic vehicle sales up 4.4% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 domestic vehicle sales up 4.4% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle sales rose 4.4 percent in calendar 1996 from a year earlier to 5,375,606 vehicles, the third successive yearly gain, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association (JADA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>JADA also said Japan's domestic vehicle sales rose 13.1 percent in December from a year earlier to 432,603 units, the fourth straight month of year-on-year gains.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of 1996 sales (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		3,711,348  up	   4.7 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc     897,986  up	   1.0 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  2,813,362  up	   6.0 percent</p>
<p> Total trucks	    1,647,031  up	   3.7 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	    168,298  down	 5.1 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  1,478,733  up	   4.8 percent</p>
<p> Buses			  17,227  down	 0.4 percent</p>
<p>The 1996 sales included 427,526 imported vehicles, up 10.1 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>Sales by Japanese makers in 1996 were as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     2,104,797  up	  3.7 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor     1,098,394  up	  0.2 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	  539,573  up	 39.9 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors  476,555  down	4.1 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	  285,204  down	8.0 percent</p>
<p> Fuji Heavy	   137,113  down	2.7 percent</p>
<p> Isuzu Motors	 136,645  down	3.1 percent</p>
<p> Suzuki Motor	  65,899  up	  8.5 percent</p>
<p> Hino Motors	   47,119  down	2.7 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Diesel	 31,947  down	9.3 percent</p>
<p> Daihatsu Motor	24,834  up	 46.7 percent</p>
<p>The figures announced on Monday were preliminary. Final figures will be announced on January 9, but these rarely differ from preliminary figures, a JADA official said.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of December sales figures (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		304,864  up   16.2 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc    78,349  up   10.7 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  226,515  up   18.1 percent</p>
<p> Trucks		    126,628  up    6.3 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	   11,764  up    7.0 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  114,864  up    6.3 percent</p>
<p> Buses			 1,111  up   11.5 percent</p>
<p>December sales included 38,060 imported vehicles, down 2.1 percent from a year before.</p>
</text>
